              176.0,
              1979.0
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "Polyacetylene and its homologues have been studied as organic semiconductors [1–3], membranes for gas separation and for liquid-mixture separation [4], chiro-optical materials [5,6], side-chain liquid crystals [7–9], materials for chemical sensors [10], and materials for nonlinear optical property [11,12] and photoluminescence and electroluminescence properties [13–17].",
          "block_bbox": [
            163,
            2030,
            1183,
            2379
          ],
          "block_id": 13,
          "block_order": 8,
          "group_id": 13,
          "block_polygon_points": [
            [
              163.0,
              2030.0
            ],
            [
              1183.0,
              2030.0
            ],
            [
              1183.0,
              2379.0
            ],
            [
              163.0,
              2379.0
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "Polyacetylenes with ionic nature have potential as materials for mixed ionic and electronic conductivities, energy storage devices such as batteries and permselective membrane, and light-emitting devices due to the their extensive conjugation and various functionalities [2,18]. The synthesis of simple mono- and disubstituted ionic polyacetylenes from ethynylpyridines had been carried out with the activation of the acetylene bond in ethynylpyridines [18,19]. We have also studied on the synthesis and characterization of the poly(2-ethynylpyridine)-based conjugated polymers having various functionalities [2,9,14].\nIn this paper, we report the synthesis of novel ionic conjugated polymers having different counter-anion (iodide, tetraphenylborate) and the characterization of resulting ionic conjugated polymers.",
          "block_bbox": [
            163,
            2380,
            1184,
            2932
          ],
          "block_id": 14,
          "block_order": 9,
          "group_id": 14,
