          ]
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "The conjugated ionic polymer, poly(2-ethynyl-N-methylpyridinium iodide) (PEMPI) was prepared by the direct polymerization of 2-ethynylpyridine with methyl iodide without any initiator system in methanol solvent. The polymerization was performed at 70 °C after standing for 1 h because of the low boiling temperature of methyl iodide. Another ionic polymer, poly(2-ethynyl-N-methyl-pyridinium tetraphenylborate) (PEMPTPB) was easily prepared by the ion-exchange reaction of PEMPI with sodium tetraphenylborate in methanol solvent. FT-IR spectra were obtained with a Bruker EQUINOX 55 spectrometer using a KBr pellet. NMR spectra were recorded on a Varian 500 MHz FT-NMR spectrometer (Model: Unity INOVA) in DMSO- $ d_{6} $. X-ray diffractograms were obtained with a Phillips X-ray diffractometer (Model: XPert-APD).",
          "block_bbox": [
